<div class="r-site" data-r107-page data-family="mechanism" data-modules="1,2,3,4,5,6"><div class="r-core-hero"><header class="r-intro r-intro--small"><h1>Core-Lock &amp; Modular System</h1><p>The Core-Lock clasp connects a SUIJI base to the charm you choose. Keep the piece you love and change the detail whenever you like.</p></header>{% render 'suiji-core-system-links' %}</div>{% render 'suiji-core-parts' %}<section class="r-section r-ice" id="how-it-works"><div class="r-section__heading"><h2>Change the detail. Keep the piece.</h2><p class="r-caption">Four-step operation guide · static illustration, no video.</p></div><ol class="r-steps"><li><span>01</span><h3>Press both sides</h3></li><li><span>02</span><h3>Remove the charm</h3></li><li><span>03</span><h3>Insert another charm</h3></li><li><span>04</span><h3>Check it is locked</h3></li></ol><p>Change the charm off the body and keep the loose parts together. Do not force an uncertain connection.</p></section><section class="r-section " id="engineering"><div class="r-section__heading"><h2>The work behind the connection</h2></div><p>During the later development of Core-Lock, we worked with French engineers specializing in springs to refine the spring structure, mechanics and the pressure needed to operate the clasp.</p><p>From the first prototype to the final hand finishing, we refine how each part fits, moves and feels. The purpose stays the same: to make it easy to change a detail while keeping the piece you love.</p></section><section class="r-section "><div class="r-section__heading"><h2>More ways to keep wearing it</h2></div><p>Change a charm on the same base. Move a charm to another base. Keep the clasp simple without a charm.</p><p>We think about sustainability through continued use: keeping a base you love while changing a compatible detail. The aim is to give the pieces you already own more occasions to be worn, without having to repeat every component.</p><div class="r-actions"><a class="r-button" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/pages/bases' | replace: '//', '/' }}">Explore the bases<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a><a class="r-button r-button--line" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/collections/all' | replace: '//', '/' }}">Explore the pieces<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a></div></section><aside class="r-reading"><p class="r-eyebrow">A useful next read</p><a class="r-link" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/blogs/journal/ornament-base-compatibility' | replace: '//', '/' }}">Will this ornament fit my SUIJI base?<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a><a class="r-link" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/blogs/journal/earring-ornament-necklace' | replace: '//', '/' }}">From earring motif to pendant: what has to change?<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a><a class="r-link" href="{{ routes.root_url | append: '/blogs/journal/interchangeable-jewelry-routine' | replace: '//', '/' }}">Interchangeable jewelry you never change: simplify the routine<span aria-hidden="true"> ↗</span></a></aside></div>
{%- endif -%}
